            <ArticleTitle>What scares patients about the hospital.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hospitalization usually disrupts a person's privacy, autonomy, life style, roles, and finances. This article discusses the anxieties a patient can experience related to future uncertainties, insufficient information, fear of personal incompetence, being exposed to hospital rumors, and anticipated pain. Interventions to reduce patient anxiety are suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
